# 6. Payment and Transaction Status

Every transaction must have a payment status:

- Paid
- Unpaid
- Partially Paid (optional)

Features:

- Allow users to update unpaid transactions when payment is received.
- Support partial payments if enabled.
- Display outstanding balances.
- Filter transactions by payment status.
- Record payment collection dates.
- Maintain a history of payment status changes.

### Important Rules

- Unpaid transactions must not affect actual collected wallet balances.
- Only the amount actually received should increase the selected wallet.
- When an unpaid transaction is settled, record the actual payment against the selected wallet.
- Do not create duplicate financial movements when changing a payment status.
- If a transaction is partially paid, only the collected amount should be reflected in wallet balances.

Payment status changes must be traceable and auditable.

